11. Conclusion

MLBRS v3.0 synthesises the most significant geroscience breakthroughs of 2025–2026 into a physiologically rational, staged, and computationally orchestrated doctoral research programme. Its core innovation is architectural: the mandatory Restore‑before‑Regenerate sequence; the integration of immunosenescence reversal and senomorphic modulation into the pre‑regenerative phase; the replacement of causal AI rhetoric with a verifiable generative‑forecasting‑plus‑counterfactual architecture; and an unprecedented safety infrastructure that includes suicide‑gene switches, miRNA detargeting, explicit CAR‑T pivot criteria, a comprehensive antagonism screening programme, quantitative entry thresholds for regeneration, teratoma surveillance, polypharmacy stratification, and ethical risk communication. Human healthspan extension, should it prove achievable, will emerge not from a single therapeutic breakthrough but from the disciplined, staged, and computationally informed orchestration of the multiple biological layers that together constitute the ageing phenotype. The MLBRS v3.0 framework provides the architectural blueprint for that orchestration and a concrete, fundable roadmap for the doctoral research required to begin its translation.


