Appendix A: Preclinical Antagonism and Safety Screening Protocols

A.1 In‑Vitro Organoid Antagonism Screen

Objective: To detect antagonism between Phase 1 components (butyrate, liver‑targeted mRNA, CAR‑T cells) before human deployment.

Organoid Models:

· Liver‑bone co‑culture (recapitulates senescence‑driven inter‑organ crosstalk; source: Bioactive Materials, 2025)
· iPSC‑derived cardiac organoids (cardiotoxicity screening)

Experimental Groups (n=6 per group):

1. Vehicle control
2. Butyrate (1 mM, continuous) alone
3. Liver mRNA cocktail (DLL1/FLT3L/IL‑7, 1 µg each, single transfection) alone
4. Anti‑uPAR CAR‑T cells (effector:target 2:1) alone
5. Butyrate + liver mRNA (sequential, 24 h apart)
6. Butyrate + CAR‑T (sequential, 24 h apart)
7. Liver mRNA + CAR‑T (sequential, 24 h apart)
8. Full Phase 1 sequential combination (butyrate → mRNA → CAR‑T, 24‑h intervals)
9. Full Phase 1 simultaneous combination

Readouts (72 h post‑final addition):

· IL‑6, IL‑8, TNF‑α (ELISA)
· LDH release (cytotoxicity)
· Caspase‑3 activation (apoptosis)
· Senescent cell clearance (SA‑β‑gal, p16⁺ flow cytometry)

Antagonism Criterion: >20% reduction in senescent cell clearance or >30% increase in inflammatory markers in combination groups vs. sum of individual effects.

Pass Condition: No group meets antagonism criterion.

