A.3 Aged‑Mouse Antagonism Study (12‑Week)

Animals: C57BL/6 mice, 18–24 months, both sexes, n=12/group.

Intervention Groups:

1. Saline control
2. Butyrate (oral, 0.5 g/kg/day)
3. Liver‑targeted mRNA (i.v. LNP, 0.5 mg/kg, weekly ×4)
4. Anti‑uPAR CAR‑T cells (i.v., 5×10⁶ cells, single dose)
5. Sequential Phase 1 (butyrate week 1–12; mRNA weeks 5–8; CAR‑T week 9)

Primary Outcomes: Frailty index, grip strength, VO₂ max (treadmill), LinAge2‑equivalent clock (DNA methylation array).

Secondary Outcomes: Plasma IL‑6, TNF‑α, TREC quantification, tissue p16⁺ burden.

Antagonism Detection: Non‑inferiority analysis; if combination arm shows significantly worse outcomes than at least two single‑component arms, protocol is paused.

