A.4 Preclinical Teratoma Safety Study (24‑Week)

Objective: Validate iCasp9 suicide‑switch efficacy for OSK‑induced teratoma elimination.

Animals: NSG mice, 8–12 weeks, injected subcutaneously with 1×10⁶ OSK‑expressing human fibroblasts (doxycycline‑inducible, ± iCasp9 construct).

Groups (n=10):

1. OSK + iCasp9, doxycycline water weeks 1–8, AP1903 0.4 mg/kg i.p. at week 9
2. OSK alone, same doxycycline, no AP1903
3. iCasp9 alone, no doxycycline
4. Vehicle

Endpoints: Teratoma incidence and volume (MRI at weeks 8, 10, 12, 24); OSK expression (qPCR); iCasp9 activation (cleaved caspase‑3 IHC).

Pass Condition: Zero teratomas in Group 1 at week 24, with ≥80% teratoma incidence in Group 2 confirming model validity.

