### I.2 CAR-T Pivot Criterion: Biopsy Site, Patient Selection, and Sampling Protocol

**The Problem**

Section 3.1.3 specifies a "3-month surveillance biopsy" as the trigger for CAR-T track pivoting, without specifying which tissue is biopsied, in which participants, and by what protocol.

**Biopsy Site Rationale**

Anti-uPAR CAR-T cells demonstrated the most significant off-target stromal and endothelial binding risk in intestinal tissue in the Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory (2025) preclinical work. The pivot criteria are therefore anchored to two tissue compartments:

- **Primary biopsy site: Rectosigmoid colon** (flexible sigmoidoscopy; 4 biopsies at 15–20 cm from anal verge). Selected because: (i) it is the tissue in which anti-uPAR CAR-T off-target stromal infiltration was observed preclinically; (ii) it is accessible by non-surgical endoscopic procedure; (iii) baseline biopsy is feasible at enrolment for intra-participant comparison.

- **Secondary biopsy site: Subcutaneous adipose tissue** (needle core biopsy, lateral abdominal wall). Selected because: (i) adipose senescent cell burden is a validated surrogate for systemic senolysis; (ii) it provides a complementary non-epithelial tissue readout; (iii) the procedure carries low morbidity.

**Patient Selection for Biopsy**

Biopsy at 3 months is performed in all CAR-T-treated participants (Track A or B), not selectively. This is non-negotiable from a safety monitoring perspective given the first-in-kind nature of the intervention. The baseline biopsy (pre-CAR-T) serves as the intra-participant control.

**Sampling Protocol**

| Parameter | Specification |
|---|---|
| Timing | Week 12 (±1 week) post-CAR-T infusion |
| Intestinal | Flexible sigmoidoscopy; 4 biopsies at 15–20 cm; formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded |
| Adipose | Needle core biopsy, lateral abdominal wall; fresh-frozen for flow cytometry |
| Staining panel | p16^INK4a, p21^CIP1, CAR construct (anti-uPAR scFv), CD31 (endothelial), α-SMA (stromal), SA-β-gal |
| Pathology read | Blinded to treatment arm; two independent pathologists |
| Pivot trigger | >10% CAR construct+ cells co-localising with CD31+ or α-SMA+ cells in stromal/endothelial compartment |

Circulating endothelial cells (CECs) are quantified by flow cytometry (CD31+/CD34+/CD45−/CD146+ phenotype) as a non-invasive corroborating measure, consistent with the pivot criterion specified in Section 3.1.3.

